.Dd October 4, 2026
.Dt LLM-USER 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm llm-user
.Nd the two axes behind "AI" and "LLM"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Em Which \&LLM User \&Are \&We Talking About?
.Pp
The two axes behind "AI" and "LLM": which model on whose hardware, and naked
or harnessed.
.Pp
Canonical copy:
.Bl -item -compact -offset indent
.It
.Lk https://coetzeestefan.substack.com/p/which-llm-user-are-we-talking-about
.El
.Sh TERMS
Definitions in the wording of the published piece.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Naked model
A model used with only its maker's defaults around it.
.It Harness
Everything a user puts around a model on purpose: instruction files, hooks,
tools, memory, a knowledge graph.
.It Frontier model
The largest current models from the main labs, usually used through the
maker's app or API.
.It Nothing exists in a vacuum
Every behaviour a model shows was forced into existence by something, the
corpus, the training signal or the harness.
.It Markovian memory
At run time the next token depends only on what is in the context window, so
anything outside the window does not exist for the model; the weights are
fixed rules, the window is the only state.
.El
